><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>MATSUMOTO TAKASHI</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>SAEKI KAZUHIKO</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>SAGANE HIROSHI</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>KITA, MASAMI</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>MATSUMOTO, TAKASHI</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>SAEKI, KAZUHIKO</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>SAGANE, HIROSHI</name></addressbook></inventor></inventors></parties></bibliographic-data><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="EN"><p>A resin composition capable of laser marking which comprises a polyolefin resin compounded with an ingredient sensitive to a laser light, such as carbon black or a white metal compound pigment, together with a dispersant, e.g., a higher fatty acid compound. Examples of the polyolefin resin include polypropylene. The resin composition may contain an elastomer in an amount of about 0.5 to 30 parts by weight per 100 parts by weight of the polyolefin resin. A surface of a molded article obtained from the resin composition is irradiated with a laser light, whereby a bright marking having an even contrast can be formed on the surface.</p></abstract><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="FR"><p>La présente invention concerne une composition résinique acceptant le marquage au laser. Cette composition réunit en un composé une résine polyoléfinique et un ingrédient sensible à la lumière laser tel que le noir de carbone ou un pigment à base de composé métallique blanc. La composition comprend également un dispersant tel qu'un composé à base d'acide gras supérieur. Parmi les polyoléfines considérées, on compte notamment les polypropylènes. La composition résinique peut contenir un élastomère représentant 0,5% à 30% de la masse de résine polyoléfinique. En exposant à la lumière laser la surface d'un article moulé réalisé dans la composition résinique de l'invention, on arrive à réaliser sur cette surface un marquage clair présentant un contraste régulier.</p></abstract><copyright>User acknowledges that the Information Retrieval Facility (IRF) and its third party providers retain all right, title and interest in and to this xml under applicable copyright laws. User acquires no ownership rights to this xml including but not limited to its format. User hereby accepts the terms and conditions of the Licence Agreement set forth at http://www.ir-facility.org/legal/marec/data_licence</copyright></patent-document>